### 8. Machine Learning Development Standards

For every ML module:

1. Define the prediction or ranking objective.
2. Identify available features and target labels.
3. Inspect missing values and data quality.
4. Perform suitable preprocessing.
5. Prevent target leakage and temporal leakage.
6. Create appropriate training, validation, and test datasets.
7. Establish a simple baseline.
8. Train and compare suitable models.
9. Evaluate using relevant metrics.
10. Save the trained model and preprocessing pipeline.
11. Expose predictions through backend APIs.
12. Record prediction timestamps and model versions.
13. Explain important predictions.
14. Monitor model performance and data drift where feasible.

Never fabricate model results.

If there is insufficient labelled data, implement a transparent rule-based baseline and clearly identify ML functionality as experimental or planned.

Use MLflow for experiment tracking when model experimentation becomes substantial.

